  "description": "Contracts of the EraTech MCP (Model Context Protocol) client: McpServerConnection (transport, URL, auth kind, headers, stdio command, tool allow-list; never a secret), IMcpCredentialResolver (secrets supplied by the app at call time), IMcpClientFactory, IMcpClientSession, IMcpSessionProvider, IMcpToolProvider (MCP tools as Microsoft.Extensions.AI AIFunctions), the tool catalog cache contract and a secret-free connection fingerprint. No MCP SDK dependency.",
